{#
| Variable                   | Type         | Description                                              |
|----------------------------|--------------|----------------------------------------------------------|
| component                  | object       | merchant settings from twilight.json                     |
| component.title_highlight  | string       | heading's leading word(s) — same colour since the revamp |
| component.title            | string       | heading rest                                             |
| component.subtitle         | string       | line under the heading                                   |
| component.use_real_reviews | bool         | the store's real reviews, every written one (default on) |
| component.items            | Collection[] | mock reviews (name, role → the grey line, text, stars) — shown when the switch is off or the store has none |
| component.two_rows         | bool         | two counter-scrolling rows on desktop (default on)       |
| component.speed            | int          | seconds for one card to pass (default 9)                 |
| component.pause_on_hover   | bool         | stop the rows under a mouse (default off)                |
| position                   | int          | sorting block                                            |

Figma "Qusah Re-Vamp": desktop 326:1655 (1400 frame at x 20; the rows run to
the page edges, two of them, counter-scrolling, a blurred white fade on each
side), mobile 290:8617 (one row, the middle card centred). Latafa's
testimonials, sized for this file.

Nothing here moves or fills by itself: qissa-testimonials.js (run by home.js)
builds VIRTUAL rows — only the cards that fit, recycled as they scroll out,
filled from the store's reviews page by page — so every written review can
pass through without the page growing. The rows have fixed heights, so the
section never shifts while the reviews load; the card shells show first.

The mock reviews ride in an inert <template> (Twig-escaped text, never run)
and are copied to a plain array first: on Salla the collection is a one-shot
iterable (the first list operation consumes it — see Latafa's testimonials).
#}
{% set real     = component.use_real_reviews is not defined or component.use_real_reviews is null or component.use_real_reviews %}
{% set two_rows = component.two_rows is not defined or component.two_rows is null or component.two_rows %}

{% set mock = [] %}
{% for item in component.items %}
    {% if item.text %}{% set mock = mock|merge([item]) %}{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

<section class="s-block qtest" id="qtest-{{ position }}" data-qtest
         {%- if real %} data-qtest-real{% endif %}
         {%- if component.pause_on_hover %} data-qtest-pause{% endif %}
         data-qtest-speed="{{ component.speed ?: 9 }}"
         data-qtest-anon="{{ trans('blocks.qissa.customer') }}"
         {%- if not real and not mock|length %} hidden{% endif %}>
    <div class="container">

        <div class="qtest__head">
            <h2 class="qtest__title">
                <span class="qtest__title-hl">{{ component.title_highlight }}</span> {{ component.title }}
            </h2>
            {% if component.subtitle %}
                <p class="qtest__subtitle">{{ component.subtitle }}</p>
            {% endif %}
        </div>

        {# row two runs the other way; phones show row one only. data-phase =
           where each row starts on desktop, as the frame draws them (px past
           the right edge) — phones centre the second card instead #}
        <div class="qtest__rows">
            <div class="qtest__viewport" data-qtest-row data-dir="1" data-phase="194.39"><div class="qtest__track"></div></div>
            {% if two_rows %}
                <div class="qtest__viewport qtest__viewport--second" data-qtest-row data-dir="-1" data-phase="11.56"><div class="qtest__track"></div></div>
            {% endif %}
            <span class="qtest__fade qtest__fade--left" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="qtest__fade qtest__fade--right" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </div>

    </div>

    {# one card — the script clones it into the rows' slots #}
    <template data-qtest-card>
        <figure class="qtest__card">
            <div class="qtest__quote-wrap">
                <blockquote class="qtest__quote" data-f="text"></blockquote>
                <hr class="qtest__divider">
            </div>
            {# rtl: the name first (right), the stars last (left) #}
            <figcaption class="qtest__foot">
                <div class="qtest__who">
                    <p class="qtest__name" data-f="name"></p>
                    <p class="qtest__meta" data-f="meta"></p>
                </div>
                {# the star (290:8636, Latafa 34:6730): filled AND stroked in one colour #}
                <div class="qtest__stars" role="img" data-f="stars">{% for n in [1, 2, 3, 4, 5] %}<svg class="qtest__star" viewBox="0 0 13.9931 13.9931" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6.7196 1.33809C6.74515 1.28647 6.78462 1.24301 6.83356 1.21263C6.8825 1.18225 6.93895 1.16615 6.99655 1.16615C7.05415 1.16615 7.1106 1.18225 7.15954 1.21263C7.20848 1.24301 7.24795 1.28647 7.2735 1.33809L8.62033 4.06616C8.70906 4.24572 8.84003 4.40107 9.00201 4.51887C9.16399 4.63667 9.35213 4.71341 9.55029 4.74249L12.5623 5.18328C12.6194 5.19155 12.673 5.21562 12.7171 5.25278C12.7612 5.28993 12.794 5.33869 12.8119 5.39353C12.8297 5.44837 12.8318 5.5071 12.818 5.56309C12.8042 5.61908 12.775 5.67009 12.7337 5.71035L10.5555 7.83147C10.4118 7.97146 10.3043 8.14427 10.2423 8.33501C10.1802 8.52575 10.1654 8.72871 10.1992 8.92643L10.7135 11.9233C10.7235 11.9803 10.7174 12.0391 10.6957 12.0928C10.674 12.1465 10.6376 12.193 10.5908 12.2271C10.5439 12.2611 10.4884 12.2813 10.4306 12.2853C10.3728 12.2893 10.3151 12.277 10.2639 12.2498L7.57143 10.8342C7.39402 10.741 7.19664 10.6923 6.99626 10.6923C6.79588 10.6923 6.59849 10.741 6.42108 10.8342L3.72916 12.2498C3.67805 12.2769 3.62036 12.289 3.56267 12.2849C3.50498 12.2808 3.4496 12.2606 3.40283 12.2266C3.35605 12.1926 3.31977 12.1461 3.29809 12.0925C3.27641 12.0389 3.27022 11.9803 3.28022 11.9233L3.79388 8.92701C3.82781 8.72921 3.81311 8.52611 3.75105 8.33525C3.68898 8.14439 3.58142 7.97149 3.43764 7.83147L1.25938 5.71093C1.21775 5.67072 1.18824 5.61963 1.17423 5.56347C1.16022 5.50731 1.16227 5.44834 1.18013 5.39329C1.198 5.33823 1.23097 5.2893 1.27528 5.25207C1.3196 5.21483 1.37348 5.1908 1.43079 5.18269L4.44223 4.74249C4.64061 4.71363 4.82901 4.637 4.99121 4.51918C5.15341 4.40136 5.28455 4.2459 5.37335 4.06616L6.7196 1.33809Z" fill="currentColor" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.16609" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>{% endfor %}</div>
            </figcaption>
        </figure>
    </template>

    {# the merchant's mock reviews, as data #}
    <template data-qtest-mock>
        {%- for item in mock -%}
            <p data-name="{{ item.name }}" data-meta="{{ item.role }}" data-stars="{{ item.stars ?: 5 }}">{{ item.text }}</p>
        {%- endfor -%}
    </template>
</section>
